on</h3>\n              <p>Sermilik Fjord was once thought to be filled with frigid Arctic water. Researchers have now shown that a deep layer of warm water from the Atlantic is infiltrating all the way to Helheim&rsquo;s face, a 100-kilometer journey.</p>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"step\">\n              <h3>3. An opening</h3>\n              <p>This summer, a mixture of subsurface melt and warm Atlantic water led to a weekslong pool of open water at Helheim&rsquo;s face&ndash;a rare chance to probe the fjord&rsquo;s depths.</p>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"step\">\n              <h3>4. Turbulent mix</h3>\n              <p>At Helheim&rsquo;s base, a channel of meltwater flushes into the fjord. This meltwater, naturally light, drags warm Atlantic water up along Helheim&rsquo;s face.</p>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </section>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n    <figcaption class=\"news-article__figure__caption\"><span class=\"text-sm text-gray letter-spacing-default\"><span class=\"text-xxs text-uppercase\">C. BICKEL/<i>Science</i></span></span></figcaption>\n  </figure>\n</div>\n<p>Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetur adipiscing elit. Nulla vel odio vehicula, imperdiet nibh sed, accumsan ipsum. Morbi at lobortis est. Suspendisse id purus aliquet, pretium mi id, imperdiet metus. Duis tincidunt suscipit dolor ut vestibulum. Integer commodo, quam non finibus fermentum, purus enim tristique lorem, eget venenatis augue arcu ac nisi. Class aptent taciti sociosqu ad litora torquent per conubia nostra, per inceptos himenaeos. Curabitur malesuada tortor et tellus convallis, lobortis interdum lacus maximus.</p>\n<p>Pellentesque velit orci, cursus vel consectetur ut, scelerisque dictum ex. Nulla id tortor nec nibh molestie molestie. In ut elementum orci. Morbi vitae diam eros. Donec facilisis egestas faucibus. Pellentesque gravida lectus ligula, eget dignissim justo vehicula tristique. Mauris elementum tempus diam eu pharetra.