v>\n            <div class=\"step\">\n              <h2>Step 2</h2>\n              <p>After a series of volcanic eruptions in the 1700s covered their wheat fields with a thick layer of ash, farmers on Lanzarote in the Canary Islands discovered that the ash kept the soil at the perfect temperature for grapevines, once they dug down a bit. One variety grown here, the endemic Malvasía Volcánica grape, produces small batch wines that are celebrated throughout Europe.</p>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"step\">\n              <h2>Step 3</h2>\n              <p>The largest sheep sale in the world takes place every Thursday (save holidays) at the Wagga Wagga Livestock Marketing Centre in New South Wales in Australia, where nearly 2 million sheep are bought and sold each year. Australia’s lamb exports have surged as global demand for meat continues to rise, with China a major market.</p>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </section>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n    <figcaption class=\"news-article__figure__caption\"><span class=\"text-sm text-gray letter-spacing-default\"><span class=\"text-xxs text-uppercase\">C. BICKEL/<i>Science</i></span></span></figcaption>\n  </figure>\n</div>\n<p>Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetur adipiscing elit. Nulla vel odio vehicula, imperdiet nibh sed, accumsan ipsum. Morbi at lobortis est. Suspendisse id purus aliquet, pretium mi id, imperdiet metus. Duis tincidunt suscipit dolor ut vestibulum. Integer commodo, quam non finibus fermentum, purus enim tristique lorem, eget venenatis augue arcu ac nisi. Class aptent taciti sociosqu ad litora torquent per conubia nostra, per inceptos himenaeos. Curabitur malesuada tortor et tellus convallis, lobortis interdum lacus maximus.</p>\n<p>Pellentesque velit orci, cursus vel consectetur ut, scelerisque dictum ex. Nulla id tortor nec nibh molestie molestie. In ut elementum orci. Morbi vitae diam eros. Donec facilisis egestas faucibus. Pellentesque gravida lectus ligula, eget dig